1 ripe banana
155g light brown sugar
½ cup / 1 stick unsalted butter, melted
1 egg
1 teaspoon vanilla extract
½ teaspoon baking soda
2 teaspoon cinnamon powder
½ teaspoon salt
160g flour
1 bag chocolate chips
flaky sea salt

Preheat your oven to 350°F and line a baking sheet with parchment paper. 
Add the banana to a bowl and mash it until smooth. 
Add the melted butter and brown sugar; mix.
Add egg, vanilla extract, baking soda, cinnamon, and salt; mix.
Add the flour and fold using a spatula. If the dough is too wet, add more flour, 1 tablespoon at a time. 
Fold in the chocolate chips.
Bake for 10-12 minutes until the edges start getting golden. 
Remove the cookies from the oven, add flaky salt, let them rest for 5 minutes before handling and eating.
